    <dcterms:abstract>The quantum discrete Liouville model in the strongly cou- pled regime, 1 &lt; c &lt; 25, is formulated as a well deﬁned quantum me- chanical problem with unitary evolution operator. The theory is self- dual: there are two exponential ﬁelds related by Hermitean conjugation, satisfying two discrete quantum Liouville equations, and living in mu- tually commuting subalgebras of the quantum algebra of observables.</dcterms:abstract>
