    <dcterms:abstract>We formulate a conjectural p-adic analogue of Borel’s theorem re- lating regulators for higher K-groups of number ﬁelds to special values of the corresponding ζ-functions, using syntomic regulators and p-adic L-functions. We also formulate a corresponding conjecture for Artin motives, and state a conjecture about the precise relation between the p-adic and classical situa- tions. Parts of the conjectures are proved when the number ﬁeld (or Artin motive) is Abelian over the rationals, and all conjectures are veriﬁed numeri- cally in some other cases.</dcterms:abstract>
