    <dcterms:abstract>We show that the set of cusp shapes of hyperbolic tunnel number one manifolds is dense in the Teichm¨uller space of the torus. A similar result holds for tunnel number n manifolds. As a consequence, for ﬁxed n, there are inﬁnitely many hyperbolic tunnel number n manifolds with at most one exceptional Dehn ﬁlling. This is in contrast to large volume Berge knots, which are tunnel number one manifolds, but with cusp shapes converging to a single point in Teichm¨uller space.</dcterms:abstract>
