    <dcterms:abstract>Multi-dimensional state-integrals of products of Faddeev’s quantum diloga- rithms arise frequently in Quantum Topology, quantum Teichm¨uller theory and complex Chern–Simons theory. Using the quasi-periodicity property of the quantum dilogarithm, we evaluate 1-dimensional state-integrals at rational points and express the answer in terms of the Rogers dilogarithm, the cyclic (quantum) dilogarithm and ﬁnite state-sums at roots of unity. We illustrate our results with the evaluation of the state-integrals of the 41, 52 and (−2, 3, 7) pretzel knots at rational points.</dcterms:abstract>
