    <dcterms:abstract>The Cottingham formula expresses the lead- ing contribution of the electromagnetic interaction to the proton-neutron mass diﬀerence as an integral over the forward Compton amplitude. Since quarks and glu- ons reggeize, the dispersive representation of this ampli- tude requires a subtraction. We assume that the asymp- totic behaviour is dominated by Reggeon exchange. This leads to a sum rule that expresses the subtraction function in terms of measurable quantities. The evalua- tion of this sum rule leads to mp−n QED = 0.58 ± 0.16 MeV.</dcterms:abstract>
