    <dcterms:title>On the regularity of critical points for O’Hara’s knot energies: From smoothness to analyticity</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:creator>Vorderobermeier, Nicole</dcterms:creator>
    <dcterms:issued>D:20211110</dcterms:issued>
    <dcterms:identifier xsi:type="dcterms:URI">https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.13129</dcterms:identifier>
    <dcterms:abstract>We prove the analyticity of smooth critical points for O’Hara’s knot energies Eα,p, with p = 1 and 2 &lt; α &lt; 3, subject to a ﬁxed length constraint. This implies, together with the main result in [BR13], that bounded energy critical points of Eα,1 subject to a ﬁxed length constraint are not only C∞but also analytic. Our approach is based on Cauchy’s method of majorants and a decomposition of the gradient that was adapted from the Möbius energy case E2,1 in [BV19].</dcterms:abstract>
    <dcterms:type>article-journal</dcterms:type>
  </metadata>
